refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Time\DurationTime\Duration::negate
Returns a duration of the same length with the opposite sign: a positive duration becomes negative, and a negative duration becomes positive. Negating a duration of zero returns a duration of zero, which is never negative.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::negate example


<?php
$duration = Time\Duration::fromSeconds(30);

var_dump($duration->negate()->negative);
var_dump($duration->negate()->negate()->negative);

// A zero duration has no sign.
var_dump(Time\Duration::fromSeconds(0)->negate()->negative);


   &example.outputs;


bool(true)
bool(false)
bool(false)
